cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HSquared.jl (or the R twin hsquared), please cite it as below."
title: "HSquared.jl: sparse quantitative-genetic modelling in Julia"
abstract: >-
  Julia engine twin of the R package hsquared for open, sparse,
  inheritance-aware quantitative genetics (animal models, relationship
  matrices, REML/ML, breeding values, and planned genomic / non-standard
  inheritance surfaces). Twin DOI pending (hub D-23); cite both repositories
  together once the shared DOI is deposited after Julia General registration.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nakagawa
    given-names: Shinichi
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7765-5182"
    email: itchyshin@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/itchyshin/HSquared.jl"
url: "https://itchyshin.github.io/HSquared.jl/"
# Matches Project.toml. Twin DOI still pending (hub D-23) — do not invent
# identifiers.doi until the Zenodo deposit after both twins are tagged v0.6.0.
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-09-02
keywords:
  - quantitative genetics
  - animal model
  - heritability
  - REML
  - pedigree
  - Julia
  - mixed models
